      {
        "fontSize": "large",
        "text": "How to make a sound play in a certain range:",
        "type": "description",
        "width": 2
      },
      {
        "fontSize": "medium",
        "text": "\nIf you want a sound to play when you enter a certain range please follow these instructions.\n\nMelee Range: \n\nPress on the Conditions tab, go to the bottom of Condition 3 and press \"Add Property Change\"\n\nThis will make a new box come up, that says \"and\" above it. Select these options\n\nSound  -  Play  -  *Sound of your choice*  - Master\n\nFor all other ranges use the exact same method just using a different condition instead of \"Condition 3\".\n\nDead Zone = Condition 5\n\nSweet Spot = Condition 6\n\nYou can find the rest by looking at the conditions colour.\n\nFrom testing this appears to work with any of the ranges.\n",
        "type": "description",
        "width": 2
      },
      {
        "fontSize": "large",
        "text": "\nChanging Colour:",
        "type": "description",
        "width": 2
      },
      {
        "fontSize": "medium",
        "text": "\nFind the condition that you want to change the colour, click on the little square of the colour and pick the colour you want.\n\nIf this doesnt make sense please read the above regarding sound.\n\n",
        "type": "description",
        "width": 2
      },
      {
        "fontSize": "large",
        "text": "\nChanging Size:",
        "type": "description",
        "width": 2
      },
      {
        "fontSize": "medium",
        "text": "\nClick on the Display Tab\n\nIn Position Settings change the Width and Height\n\n\n\n\nContact me on Discord if you have any questions Smarnz#6696",
        "type": "description",
        "width": 2
      }
